{"cuisine/cuisine-of-the-western-united-states":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/cuisine-of-the-western-united-states","n":"Western American cuisine","c":"#94bd5c","crumb":[["The Americas","cuisines#the-americas"],["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine"]],"sub":"Regional cuisine in United States of America","intro":[["The Western United States has its cuisine, distinct in various ways from that of the rest of the country. States west of Texas, Kansas, Missouri, and Nebraska would be considered part of this area, as would, in some cases, western parts of adjoining states."],["The locavore movement is increasingly influential, as is the concept of sustainability. The influence of the Native American cultures of each area, but especially in the Northwest and in Navajo country, is important in the cuisine picture of the Western United States."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"cuisine-of-the-western-united-states"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cuisine_of_the_Western_United_States"}],"sections":[{"h":"Dishes","count":3,"links":[["Crab Louie","dish/crab-louie"],["Dutch baby pancake","dish/dutch-baby-pancake"],["Seattle-style hot dog","dish/seattle-style-hot-dog"]]},{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Key ingredients","links":[["Asparagus","ingredient/asparagus"],["Crab meat","ingredient/crab-meat"],["Hard-boiled egg","ingredient/hard-boiled-egg"],["Iceberg lettuce","ingredient/iceberg-lettuce"],["Louis dressing","ingredient/louis-dressing"],["Tomato","ingredient/tomato"],["Cinnamon","ingredient/cinnamon"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Milk","ingredient/milk"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Vanilla","ingredient/vanilla"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"],["Bialy","ingredient/bialy"],["Bialy (bread)","ingredient/bialy-bread"],["Cream cheese","ingredient/cream-cheese"],["Hot dog","ingredient/hot-dog"],["Hot dog bun","ingredient/hot-dog-bun"],["Sautéed onions","ingredient/sauteed-onions"]],"note":"Most used across its dishes."},{"h":"Part of","links":[["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Within Western American cooking","count":4,"links":[["Cuisine of California","cuisine/cuisine-of-california"],["Hawaiian cuisine","cuisine/cuisine-of-hawaii"],["Pacific Northwest cuisine","cuisine/pacific-northwest-cuisine"],["Rocky Mountain cuisine","cuisine/rocky-mountain-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"Cuisine of the Americas","img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/b/b4/Chez_Panisse_pizza.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"stu_spivack","lic":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chez_Panisse_pizza.jpg"}},"cuisine/maharashtrian-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/maharashtrian-cuisine","n":"Maharashtrian cuisine","c":"#f0b340","crumb":[["Asia","cuisines#asia"],["Indian cuisine","cuisine/indian-cuisine"]],"sub":"Regional cuisine in India","intro":[["Maharashtrian or Marathi cuisine is the cuisine of the Marathi people from the Indian state of Maharashtra. It has distinctive attributes, while sharing much with other Indian cuisines. Traditionally, Maharashtrians have considered their food to be more austere than others."],["Maharashtrian cuisine includes mild and spicy dishes. Wheat, rice, jowar, bajri, vegetables, lentils and fruit are dietary staples. Peanuts and cashews are often served with vegetables. Meat was traditionally used sparsely or only by the well-off until recently, because of economic conditions and culture."],["The urban population in metropolitan cities of the state has been influenced by cuisine from other parts of India and abroad. For example, the South Indian dishes idli and dosa, as well as Chinese and Western dishes such as pizza, are popular in home cooking and in restaurants."],["Distinctly Maharashtrian dishes include ukdiche modak, aluchi patal bhaji, kanda pohe and thalipeeth."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"maharashtrian-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maharashtrian_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Dishes","count":3,"links":[["Pav bhaji","dish/pav-bhaji"],["Usal","dish/usal"],["Vada pav","dish/vada-pav"]]},{"h":"Recipe sites","count":2,"rows":[{"name":"Shweta in the Kitchen (Maharashtrian)","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"shwetainthekitchen.com","note":"Maharashtrian section of an Indian home cooking blog.","url":"https://shwetainthekitchen.com/category/maharashtrian/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Tarla Dalal (Maharashtrian)","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"tarladalal.com","note":"Maharashtrian category on Tarla Dalal's long-running recipe site.","url":"https://www.tarladalal.com/recipes/category/Maharashtrian/?page=3","suggested":true,"kind":"site"}]},{"h":"Cookbooks","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"Ruchira: Selected Maharashtrian Vegetarian Recipes","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Kamalabai Ogale","note":"English edition of the best-known Marathi household cookbook.","url":"","suggested":true}]},{"h":"Key ingredients","links":[["Bread roll","ingredient/bread-roll"],["Lentil","ingredient/lentil"],["Batata vada","ingredient/batata-vada"]],"note":"Most used across its dishes."},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Indian cuisine","cuisine/indian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Within Maharashtrian cooking","count":1,"links":[["Hridhaansh cuisine","cuisine/hridhaansh-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"Asian cuisine","img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/6/63/Pav_Bhaji.jpg/500px-Pav_Bhaji.jpg","w":500,"h":667,"by":"Rishika Palvankar","lic":"CC BY 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pav_Bhaji.jpg","of":"Pav bhaji"}},"cuisine/samoan-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/samoan-cuisine","n":"Samoan cuisine","c":"#55b8ad","crumb":[["Oceania","cuisines#oceania"],["Cuisine"]],"sub":"National cuisine of Samoa","intro":[["The traditional culture of Samoa is a communal way of life based on Fa'a Samoa, the unique socio-political culture. In Samoan culture, most activities are done together. The traditional living quarters, or fale (houses), contain no walls and up to 20 people may sleep on the ground in the same fale. During the day, the fale is used for chatting and relaxing. One's family is viewed as an integral part of a person's life. The aiga or extended family lives and works together. Elders in the family are greatly respected and hold the highest status, and this may be seen at a traditional Sunday umu (normal oven)."],["Samoan culture is present in both the Independent State of Samoa and in American Samoa (a territory of the United States)."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"samoan-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Samoan_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"Polynesian Cultural Center Blog: Samoan recipes","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"blog.polynesia.com","note":"Samoan dishes such as palusami from the Hawaii cultural center's blog, written with its Pacific Islander staff.","url":"https://blog.polynesia.com/tag/samoan-recipe","suggested":true,"kind":"site"}]},{"h":"Cookbooks","count":2,"rows":[{"name":"Mea'ai Samoa: Recipes and Stories from the Heart of Polynesia","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Robert Oliver, Tracy Berno and Shiri Ram, 2013","note":"Samoa-focused follow-up to Me'a Kai, tracing dishes back to local growers; won a Gourmand award.","url":"https://openlibrary.org/isbn/9781775534273","suggested":true,"isbn":"9781775534273"},{"name":"Me'a Kai: The Food and Flavours of the South Pacific","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Robert Oliver, Tracy Berno and Shiri Ram, 2010","note":"Regional cookbook with a chapter of Samoan recipes from island cooks.","url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL28452199M","suggested":true,"isbn":"9781869621759"}]}],"cont":"Oceanic cuisine","img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/b/b7/DSC00951_Culture_of_Samoa.jpg/500px-DSC00951_Culture_of_Samoa.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"Claire Charters","lic":"CC BY 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:DSC00951_Culture_of_Samoa.jpg"}},"dish/fish-and-chips":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/fish-and-chips","n":"Fish and chips","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 10 cuisines","dot":"#e46a3f","intro":[["Fish and chips is a hot dish consisting of battered and fried fish served with chips. Often considered the national dish of the United Kingdom, fish and chips originated in England in the 19th century. Today, the dish is a common takeaway food in numerous other countries, particularly English-speaking and Commonwealth nations."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-fish-and-chips"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fish_and_chips"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Afrikaner cuisine","cuisine/afrikaner-cuisine"],["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine"],["Australian cuisine","cuisine/australian-cuisine"],["Canadian cuisine","cuisine/canadian-cuisine"],["English cuisine","cuisine/english-cuisine"],["Indian cuisine","cuisine/indian-cuisine"],["Irish cuisine","cuisine/irish-cuisine"],["New Zealand cuisine","cuisine/new-zealand-cuisine"],["Norwegian cuisine","cuisine/norwegian-cuisine"],["South African cuisine","cuisine/south-african-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":6,"links":[["Atlantic cod","ingredient/atlantic-cod"],["Fish","ingredient/fish"],["French fries","ingredient/french-fries"],["Fried fish","ingredient/fried-fish"],["Fries","ingredient/fries"],["Potato","ingredient/potato"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Belly Rumbles: Australian Recipes","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"bellyrumbles.com","note":"Sara McCleary's collection of Australian classics such as Anzac biscuits, pavlova, sausage rolls and native-ingredient bakes.","url":"https://bellyrumbles.com/category/australian-recipes/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"RecipeTin Eats","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"recipetineats.com","note":"Sydney-based Nagi Maehashi's widely used recipe site; broad in scope, but a staple of Australian home cooking.","url":"https://www.recipetineats.com/home/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Kitchen Frau: Canadian Food","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"kitchenfrau.com","note":"Canadian food section of an Alberta-based home cooking blog.","url":"https://www.kitchenfrau.com/canadian-food/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Swasthi's Recipes","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"indianhealthyrecipes.com","note":"Swasthi Shreekanth's long-running blog of everyday Indian home cooking from across the regions.","url":"https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/about/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Afrikaner cuisine","links":[["Bobotie","dish/bobotie"],["Hertzoggie","dish/hertzoggie"],["Malva pudding","dish/malva-pudding"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/7/76/Fish_and_chips.jpg/500px-Fish_and_chips.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"© Andrew Dunn, http://www.andrewdunnphoto.com/","lic":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fish_and_chips.jpg"}},"ingredient/creme-fraiche":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/creme-fraiche","n":"Crème fraîche","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 4 cuisines","intro":[["Crème fraîche is a dairy product similar to sour cream; it is a soured cream containing 10–45% butterfat, with a pH of approximately 4.5. It is soured with a bacterial culture. European labeling regulations specify the two ingredients must be cream and bacterial culture. It is served over fruit and baked goods, as well as being added to soups and sauces. It is used in a variety of other recipes. Sour cream is a similar foodstuff, except that crème fraîche is less sour and has a higher fat content. Sour cream may contain thickening agents not permitted in crème fraîche in many jurisdictions."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-creme-fraiche"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cr%C3%A8me_fra%C3%AEche"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":4,"groups":[["French cuisine","cuisine/french-cuisine",[["Flammekueche","dish/flammekueche"]]],["German cuisine","cuisine/german-cuisine",[["Flammekueche","dish/flammekueche"]]],["New Caledonian cuisine","cuisine/new-caledonian-cuisine",[["Flammekueche","dish/flammekueche"]]],["Thuringian cuisine","cuisine/german-cuisine-thuringia",[["Flammekueche","dish/flammekueche"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Bacon","ingredient/bacon"],["Cream","ingredient/cream"],["Fromage frais","ingredient/fromage-frais"],["Lardon","ingredient/lardon"],["Onion","ingredient/onion"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/a/a9/Cr%C3%A8me_d%27Isigny_2.JPG/500px-Cr%C3%A8me_d%27Isigny_2.JPG","w":500,"h":374,"by":"Patafisik","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cr%C3%A8me_d'Isigny_2.JPG"}},"dish/focaccia-pugliese":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/focaccia-pugliese","n":"Focaccia pugliese","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Italian cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Focaccia is a flat leavened oven-baked Italian bread. It is similar to a flatbread called pizza bianca in Roman cuisine."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-focaccia-pugliese"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Focaccia_pugliese"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Italian cuisine","cuisine/italian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":2,"links":[["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"],["Yeast","ingredient/yeast"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Pasta Grannies","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"pastagrannies.substack.com","note":"V