Scottish cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Haggis pakora is a Scottish snack food that combines traditional Scottish haggis ingredients with the spices, batter and preparation method of pakora from the Indian subcontinent. It has become a popular food in Indian and Pakistani restaurants in Scotland, and is also available in prepared form in supermarkets."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-haggis-pakora"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haggis_pakora"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Scottish cuisine","cuisine/scottish-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":8,"links":[["Besan","ingredient/besan"],["Gram flour","ingredient/gram-flour"],["Haggis","ingredient/haggis"],["Oatmeal","ingredient/oatmeal"],["Offal","ingredient/offal"],["Onion","ingredient/onion"],["Suet","ingredient/suet"],["Yogurt","ingredient/yogurt"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Scottish Scran","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"scottishscran.com","note":"Blog working through traditional Scottish dishes one recipe at a time.","url":"https://scottishscran.com","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Something Sweet Something Savoury: Scottish recipes","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"somethingsweetsomethingsavoury.com","note":"Scottish home baking and cooking section of a UK food blog.","url":"https://somethingsweetsomethingsavoury.com/category/scottish-recipes/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Scottish cuisine","links":[["Clootie dumpling","dish/clootie-dumpling"],["Cock-a-leekie","dish/cock-a-leekie"],["Finnan haddie","dish/finnan-haddie"],["Haggis","dish/haggis"],["Hobnob biscuit","dish/hobnob-biscuit"],["Lorne sausage","dish/lorne-sausage"],["Mince and tatties","dish/mince-and-tatties"],["Rumbledethumps","dish/rumbledethumps"],["Scotch broth","dish/scotch-broth"],["Skirlie","dish/skirlie"],["Stornoway black pudding","dish/stornoway-black-pudding"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/d/d5/Haggis_pakora.jpg/500px-Haggis_pakora.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Aymatth2","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Haggis_pakora.jpg"}},"ingredient/mandu":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/mandu","n":"Mandu","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Mandu, or mandoo, are dumplings in Korean cuisine. Mandu can be steamed, boiled, pan-fried, or deep-fried. The styles also vary across regions in the Korean Peninsula. Mandu were long part of Korean royal court cuisine, but are now found in supermarkets, restaurants, and snack places such as pojangmacha and bunsikjip throughout South Korea."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-mandu"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mandu_(food)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Korean cuisine","cuisine/korean-cuisine",[["Mandu-guk","dish/mandu-guk"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Mandu (dumpling)","ingredient/mandu-dumpling"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/0/0c/%EB%A7%8C%EB%91%90.jpg/500px-%EB%A7%8C%EB%91%90.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Raven9722","lic":"CC0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%EB%A7%8C%EB%91%90.jpg"}},"dish/mesir-macunu":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/mesir-macunu","n":"Mesir macunu","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Turkish cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Mesir Macunu is a traditional Turkish sweet associated with the city of Manisa, which holds a yearly festival to celebrate it. It consists of sugar (or honey), water, organic acid, and a blend of dozens of spices. Earlier versions of Mesir macunu were likely less sweet and more spicy in flavor."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-mesir-macunu"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mesir_macunu"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Turkish cuisine","cuisine/turkish-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":1,"links":[["Toffee","ingredient/toffee"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Ozlem's Turkish Table","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"ozlemsturkishtable.com","note":"Turkish-born cook and teacher Ozlem Warren's blog of home-style Turkish recipes.","url":"https://ozlemsturkishtable.com/tag/turkish-recipes/page/9","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Turkish cuisine","links":[["Adana kebabı","dish/adana-kebab"],["Baba ghanoush","dish/baba-ghanoush"],["Bici bici","dish/bici-bici"],["Boortsog","dish/boortsog"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Çiğ köfte","dish/cig-kofte"],["Çökertme kebabı","dish/cokertme-kebab"],["Doner kebab","dish/doner-kebab"],["Düğün çorbası","dish/dugun-corbas"],["Eggplant jam","dish/eggplant-jam"],["İmam bayıldı","dish/imam-bay-ld"],["İskender kebap","dish/iskender-kebap"],["Kavurma","dish/kavurma"],["Keşkek","dish/keskek"],["Kuru fasulye","dish/kuru-fasulye"],["Kyopolou","dish/kyopolou"],["Nevzine tatlısı","dish/nevzine-tatl-s"],["Ntolmás","dish/ntolmas"],["Pilaf","dish/pilaf"],["Piyaz","dish/piyaz"],["Qatlama","dish/qatlama"],["Rakı","dish/rak"],["Şıllık","dish/s-ll-k"],["Stuffed leaves","dish/stuffed-leaves"],["Stuffed peppers","dish/stuffed-peppers"],["Stuffed squash","dish/stuffed-squash"],["Stuffed tomatoes","dish/stuffed-tomatoes"],["Taramasalata","dish/taramasalata"],["Yayla çorbası","dish/yayla-corbas"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/8/88/Mesir_paste_of_Manisa.JPG/500px-Mesir_paste_of_Manisa.JPG","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Teemeah","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mesir_paste_of_Manisa.JPG"}},"ingredient/borassus-flabellifer":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/borassus-flabellifer","n":"Borassus flabellifer","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Borassus flabellifer, also known as palmyra palm, is a fan palm native to tropical and sub-tropical regions of South Asia and Southeast Asia. It is a tall, sturdy tree growing up to 20–30 m, with large fan-shaped leaves arranged in the form of a crown. It produces a pale white and branched inflorescence consisting of clusters of flowers. It produces bunches of large fruits containing sweet, watery kernels."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-borassus-flabellifer"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Borassus_flabellifer"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine",[["Neera","dish/neera"]]]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/3/39/Palymyra_in_Tamil_Nadu.jpg/500px-Palymyra_in_Tamil_Nadu.jpg","w":500,"h":667,"by":"Lokeswaran Kaliyappan","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Palymyra_in_Tamil_Nadu.jpg"}},"dish/sashimi":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/sashimi","n":"Sashimi","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Japanese cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Sashimi is a Japanese delicacy that consists of fresh raw fish or other raw meat that is sliced into thin pieces, and is often eaten with soy sauce."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-sashimi"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sashimi"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Japanese cuisine","cuisine/japanese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":1,"links":[["Fish","ingredient/fish"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Just One Cookbook","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"justonecookbook.com","note":"Namiko Chen's long-running blog and videos on Japanese home cooking.","url":"https://justonecookbook.com","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"RecipeTin Japan","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"japan.recipetineats.com","note":"Japanese home recipes from Yumiko, a Japan-born cook, sister site to RecipeTin Eats.","url":"https://japan.recipetineats.com/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Japanese cuisine","links":[["Bergh–Stoutenburgh House","dish/bergh-stoutenburgh-house"],["Chikuwa","dish/chikuwa"],["Curry bread","dish/curry-bread"],["Donburi","dish/donburi"],["Fukamushicha","dish/fukamushicha"],["Gyokuro","dish/gyokuro"],["Hitsumabushi","dish/hitsumabushi"],["Horumonyaki","dish/horumonyaki"],["Iekei ramen","dish/iekei-ramen"],["Inago no tsukudani","dish/inago-no-tsukudani"],["Itamae","dish/itamae"],["Izakaya","dish/izakaya"],["Japanese cheesecake","dish/japanese-cheesecake"],["Japanese noodles","dish/japanese-noodles"],["Japanese restaurant","dish/japanese-restaurant"],["Japanese tea","dish/japanese-tea"],["Jingisukan","dish/jingisukan"],["Kaki furai","dish/kaki-furai"],["Kamaboko","dish/kamaboko"],["Kōji (food)","dish/koji-food"],["Kusa mochi","dish/kusa-mochi"],["Kushikatsu","dish/kushikatsu"],["List of Japanese restaurants","dish/list-of-japanese-restaurants"],["Makizushi","dish/makizushi"],["Miso","dish/miso"],["Miso soup","dish/miso-soup"],["Monjayaki","dish/monjayaki"],["Nikujaga","dish/nikujaga"],["Nimono","dish/nimono"],["Oden","dish/oden"],["Onigiri","dish/onigiri"],["Osechi","dish/osechi"],["Oyakodon","dish/oyakodon"],["Rainbow roll","dish/rainbow-roll"],["Ramen","dish/ramen"],["Ryōtei","dish/ryotei"],["Sencha","dish/sencha"],["Shizuoka oden","dish/shizuoka-oden"],["Sumiso","dish/sumiso"],["Sushi","dish/sushi"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/b/ba/Sushi_1.JPG/500px-Sushi_1.JPG","w":500,"h":375,"by":"No machine-readable author provided. Arnaud 25 assumed (based on copyright claims).","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sushi_1.JPG"}},"ingredient/skewer":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/skewer","n":"Skewer","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["A skewer is a thin metal or wood stick used to hold pieces of food together. The word may sometimes be used as a metonym, to refer to the entire food item served on a skewer, as in \"chicken skewers\". Skewers are used while grilling or roasting meats and fish, and in other culinary applications."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-skewer"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skewer"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine",[["Sate bandeng","dish/sate-bandeng"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Banana leaf","ingredient/banana-leaf"],["Caraway seed","ingredient/caraway-seed"],["Chili pepper","ingredient/chili-pepper"],["Coconut","ingredient/coconut"],["Coconut milk","ingredient/coconut-milk"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Galangal","ingredient/galangal"],["Ginger","ingredient/ginger"],["Milkfish","ingredient/milkfish"],["Tamarind","ingredient/tamarind"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/6/62/Wooden_skewers.jpg/500px-Wooden_skewers.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Hans Braxmeier","lic":"CC0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wooden_skewers.jpg"}},"dish/youtiao":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/youtiao","n":"Youtiao","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Chinese cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Youtiao, known in Southern China as yau char kway (Chinese: 油炸鬼), is a long golden-brown deep-fried strip of wheat flour dough of Chinese origin and (by a variety of other names) also popular in other East and Southeast Asian cuisines."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-youtiao"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Youtiao"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":